{"piece_id": "la-capinera", "scope": "whole_piece", "measure_range": null, "language": "en", "answer_language": "en", "evidence_language": "ko", "retrieval_query": "이 곡의 작곡 배경은 무엇인가요?", "answer": "The composition of *La capinera* is attributed to Julius Benedict, a 19th-century British composer. The original Italian libretto is credited to Francesco Rizzelli, though the piece is also associated with an English text by F. Enoch titled \"The Bird that came in Spring,\" which was first published in D major and later reprinted in F major. The version commonly performed today includes the Italian lyrics alongside the original English text. Additionally, Benedict and Henry Bishop, both active in Britain during the 1850s, composed several songs for flute, soprano, and piano, including *La capinera*. The work is described as a virtuosic piece tailored for coloratura soprano and flute.", "generation_mode": "llm", "answer_basis": "retrieved_evidence", "unavailable_reason": null, "generation_validation_warning": "Generated answer contains an uncited substantive claim", "score_context": null, "has_primary_grounding": true, "has_selected_range_grounding": null, "has_confirmed_local_examples": true, "pipeline": "soprano_qa", "model": {"path": "Qwen3-14B-Q6_K.gguf", "checkpoint_exists": true, "backend": "llama-cpp-python"}, "retrieval": {"configured_mode": "hybrid", "active_mode": "hybrid", "dense_available": true, "embedding_model": "Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-Q8_0.gguf", "embedding_dimension": 1024, "last_dense_error": null, "last_search_mode": "hybrid", "query_route": "hybrid", "route_reason": "dense_result_returned", "ambiguous_candidates": [], "dense_attempted": true, "dense_contributed": true}, "evidence": [{"id": "la-capinera-ku-005", "piece_id": "la-capinera", "kind": "expert", "evidence_type": "expert_annotation", "usage_class": null, "topic": "", "question": "", "text": "‘o mia gentil’의 dim.은 이 가사를 더욱 표현하기 위한 지시로 보는 것이 좋겠다. 디미뉴엔도에서 작곡가가 어떤 효과를 의도했는지 생각하고, 그에 따라 뒤에 이어지는 단어들의 표현에 주의해 노래해야 한다.", "measure_ranges": [[17, 19]], "is_local": true, "measure_scope": "local", "measure_status": "specific", "scope_match": "local_example", "generation_role": "local_example", "selected_range_claim_authority": null, "in_requested_scope": true, "score": 0.457049, "text_score": 0.0, "dense_score": 0.457049, "dense_content_score": 0.443823, "fusion_score": 0.639516, "retrieval_mode": "dense", "measure_score": 1.0, "alias_score": 0.0, "concept_coverage": 0.5, "content_concept_coverage": 0.5, "answer_relation_score": 0.0, "semantic_match_type": "dense", "source_ids": ["kim-la-capinera-04"], "web_source_ids": [], "claim_ids": [], "sources": [], "generated_text_license": null, "attributions": [], "text_en": "The dim. on o mia gentil can be understood as a directive intended to express this lyric more fully. Think about the effect the composer intended with the diminuendo and sing with attention to the expression of the words that follow."}, {"id": "webchunk-8b7f3c83516f70b01ef4", "piece_id": "la-capinera", "kind": "web", "evidence_type": "web_database", "usage_class": "research_conditional", "topic": "creator_profiles", "question": "creator_profiles에 대해 알려 주세요.", "text": "1881년 악보가 싣는 이탈리아어 원시의 작사는 프란체스코 리첼리에게 귀속된다.", "measure_ranges": [], "is_local": false, "measure_scope": "global", "measure_status": null, "scope_match": "general_evidence", "generation_role": "general_support", "selected_range_claim_authority": null, "in_requested_scope": true, "score": 9.320929, "text_score": 7.820929, "dense_score": 0.455725, "dense_content_score": 0.523017, "fusion_score": 0.968254, "retrieval_mode": "hybrid", "measure_score": 1.5, "alias_score": 0.0, "concept_coverage": 1.0, "content_concept_coverage": 0.0, "answer_relation_score": 0.0, "semantic_match_type": "strict", "source_ids": [], "web_source_ids": ["websrc-9b9bb707a6ee7d12c62e", "websrc-adfc9df6ea4b6623843d"], "claim_ids": ["webclaim-481f6c16c113c6d33e2b"], "sources": [{"web_source_id": "websrc-9b9bb707a6ee7d12c62